            <ArticleTitle>Ruptured intercostal artery pseudoaneurysm: a rare cause of acute back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2015-209788</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2015209788</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 63-year-old man with no relevant medical history presented with acute non-traumatic back pain and was found to have a T8 intercostal artery pseudoaneurysm associated with haemomediastinum on CT of the chest. He was taken to angiography with interventional radiology and the aneurysm was coiled without complication.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
